WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.534
Integrating OT monitoring with a security operations center combines established alert workflows with industrial visibility.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:11.253
The SOC can provide continuous triage, correlation, case management, and escalation,

00:00:11.253 --> 00:00:14.684
while OT specialists provide the asset, protocol, process,

00:00:14.684 --> 00:00:17.687
and safety context needed for sound decisions.

00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:23.692
Forward selected OT events to the SIEM rather than every available record without purpose.

00:00:23.692 --> 00:00:28.840
Preserve useful fields such as asset identity, zone, function, protocol, command category,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.842
user, remote session, maintenance state, and criticality.

00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:35.703
Time synchronization and consistent naming are essential for correlation.

00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:39.134
Detection content should link enterprise and OT pathways.

00:00:39.134 --> 00:00:42.995
A compromised identity, VPN session, jump-host event, firewall connection,

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:46.427
and unusual controller communication may form one investigation.

00:00:46.427 --> 00:00:51.574
The SOC needs contacts and runbooks that explain who can validate each

00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:54.577
stage and which actions require operational approval.

00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:59.295
Monitoring can update asset inventory by revealing new devices, changed communication,

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:01.869
or dormant systems returning to service.

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:07.016
Vulnerability management can use observed reachability and software clues to improve prioritization.

00:01:07.016 --> 00:01:12.164
Architecture teams can compare actual traffic with approved conduits and segmentation policy.

00:01:12.164 --> 00:01:16.882
Governance should define data ownership, retention, access, alert service levels, escalation,

00:01:16.882 --> 00:01:19.027
monitoring health, and coverage gaps.

00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:22.887
Reports should communicate meaningful risk: unsupported sensors, unmonitored sites,

00:01:22.887 --> 00:01:26.319
repeated unauthorized access, baseline drift, unresolved high-consequence alerts,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.464
and time to coordinated response.

00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:34.898
Integration does not mean removing OT authority or treating industrial alerts exactly like office endpoints.

00:01:34.898 --> 00:01:37.472
It creates a shared operating model.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:40.045
Security operations contribute scale and consistency;

00:01:40.045 --> 00:01:43.906
engineering and operations contribute process knowledge and safe response.

00:01:43.906 --> 00:01:50.340
Together they turn telemetry into decisions that protect both the network and the physical mission.
